# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data: never commit raw or bulk data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public NP-MRD raw archive (experimental_spectra.zip, ~13.7 GB) lives in
# the owner's Google Drive SUMMIT workspace and in GCS -- never in git.
experimental_spectra.zip

# The SUMMIT reference implementation's workspace: model checkpoints (.pt),
# HOSE/shift tables, benchmark_v2/v3/v4 outputs, and database dumps.  These
# are the reference implementation's artifacts, useful for cross-checking
# the platform but NOT part of it (ADR-0025).  Only the small, public
# benchmark CSVs copied into tests/fixtures/real_npmrd/ are committed.
summit_poc/

# Local-only source trees (outside the repo by design; listed here so an
# accidental in-repo copy is obviously wrong):
#   /Users/<user>/Library/CloudStorage/.../My Drive/NMR-Data   [local only, do not redistribute]

# NOTE: data/inventory/*.json and data/validation_report.json ARE committed --
# they are provenance/validation records (hashes, counts, timings) containing
# no spectral data and no PII, and they are the evidence that the platform
# was validated against public data.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase / Google service credentials (Step 6.5, ADR-0028).
# NEVER commit service-account keys: they grant full project access.
firebase-service-account.json
*-credentials.json
*-service-account.json
serviceAccountKey.json
.env.local
.env.*.local

